    {
      "text": "it shall bruise thy head, Gen. 3:15 (Moses 4:21). These be the heads of their fathers’ houses, Ex. 6:14 (Num. 1:4; 7:2). made them heads over the people, Ex. 18:25. hands upon the head of the bullock, Ex. 29:10 (Lev. 8:14). shall no razor come upon his head, Num. 6:5 (Judg. 13:5). made them heads over you, captains, Deut. 1:15. he said unto his father, My head, my head, 2 Kgs. 4:19. axe head fell into the water, 2 Kgs. 6:5. fastened his head in the temple of Dagon, 1 Chr. 10:10. thou anointest my head with oil, Ps. 23:5. stone which the builders refused is become the head stone, Ps. 118:22 (Matt. 21:42; Mark 12:10; Luke 20:17; Acts 4:11; 1 Pet. 2:7). hast covered my head in the day of battle, Ps. 140:7. hoary head is a crown of glory, Prov. 16:31. heap coals of fire upon his head, Prov. 25:22 (Rom. 12:20). whole head is sick, and the whole heart faint, Isa. 1:5. Thou art this head of gold, Dan. 2:38.",
