    {
      "text": "Neither shalt thou swear by thy head, Matt. 5:36 (3 Ne. 12:36). Son … hath not where to lay his head, Matt. 8:20 (Luke 9:58). Give me here John Baptist’s head, Matt. 14:8 (Mark 6:25). crown of thorns, they put it upon his head, Matt. 27:29 (Mark 15:17; John 19:2). not my feet only, but also my hands and my head, John 13:9. head of every man is Christ; and the head of the woman is the man, 1 Cor. 11:3 (Eph. 5:23). having his head covered, dishonoureth his head, 1 Cor. 11:4. nor again the head to the feet, I have no need, 1 Cor. 12:21 (D&C 84:109). head over all things to the church, Eph. 1:22. which is the head, even Christ, Eph. 4:15. he is the head of the body, the church, Col. 1:18. head of all principality and power, Col. 2:10. not holding the Head, from which all the body … increaseth, Col. 2:19. on their heads were as it were crowns like gold, Rev. 9:7. dragon, having seven heads, Rev. 12:3. seven heads are seven mountains, Rev. 17:9.",
